"What is your name?"
"Ragnar, a Lemurian," answered the man, sitting down on soft pillows. When the chamberlain noticed how the sofa sagged under weight of his guest, he stood motionless for a moment, but in a second found himself more confident, because he was a bit taller compared to the seated Ragnar.
"People disappear in our city," started Abu Ali. "A few water carriers went missing. Apparently the beast caught them by the well, where they draw water."
"Why do you think so?"
"A few times people saw inhuman footprints there. In-hu-man, understand? The beast probably lives in the caves under the well. What will you say, mighty warrior, will you kill this creature?"
"What will be my reward?" asked Ragnar. His stern look made chamberlain shiver.
"I'm offering good money: 1000 coins." What the Lemurian heard made him smile with satisfaction.
"Great, I agree." After those words he abruptly arose from the sofa. "To prove that the job is done, I will bring back its head," said Ragnar, heading towards the exit.
Abu Ali exhaled with relief, very glad that this meeting was over. The appearance of his guest seemed by far too wild and threatening for his tastes.